# display-link.patch
#
# STATUS: BROKEN. Do not enable it expecting it to work. It is included only so
# the mode can be reproduced and debugged: after the first few frames the update
# requests stop arriving and the waveform freezes on screen. The cause is not
# understood yet.
#
# It is inert unless explicitly selected: the mode is only used when the config
# key [Waveform] VSync is set to 7. With any other value none of this code runs.
#
# What it is: an alternative frame source that takes the cadence from the
# platform (QWindow::requestUpdate(), backed by a CVDisplayLink in the Cocoa
# plugin) instead of measuring it with a PLL. Architecturally this is the right
# successor to the PLL - it cannot drift, and it follows the window from monitor
# to monitor by construction - which is why the unfinished work is kept rather
# than deleted.
#
# Contains: DisplayLinkFrameDriver, the macOS CADisplayLink wrapper, the
# ST_DISPLAY_LINK mode in VSyncThread (the thread is not started in this mode,
# it only serves as the time provider), the UpdateRequest hook in OpenGLWindow,
# and the reattach logic that moves the driver from the 3x3 shared-context
# helper window onto a real waveform window (without which nothing is drawn
# outside full screen).
#
# Independent of the PLL patches and of telemetry.patch; touches
# waveformwidgetfactory.cpp in different places than telemetry.patch does.
#
# NOT COMBINABLE with pll-drift-clamp-fixed.patch: both edit the same regions
# of vsyncthread.cpp/.h and of the ST_PLL branch in waveformwidgetfactory.cpp,
# and neither order applies (verified in both directions). With the as-built
# pll-drift-clamp.patch the stack does apply: display-link, then pll-init-fix,
# then pll-drift-clamp.
#
# Applies to: clean main 9e670c1120.
